# Auto-commit finished work

When a feature, fix, or chore in this repo is **done** (build/lint ok, no leftover WIP), create a git commit without waiting for "please commit".

- Message style: `feat:` / `fix:` / `chore:` / `docs:` / `refactor:` — short, why not what
- Author: this repo’s local identity (`pieciks`)
- Do not `git push` unless asked
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials)
- Do not commit if there is nothing to commit, or if the user said not to
- One commit per finished unit of work, not a dump of unrelated WIP
